---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Ask from '../components/Ask.astro';

const cards = [
  {
    num: '01', img: '/images/transfers/pardo-50-anchored.jpg', alt: 'A black Pardo day boat lying at anchor on flat water, sunpads and seating laid out on deck',
    h: 'Why go private', tag: 'The travel day, upgraded',
    bestfor: 'Best for · honeymoons, short trips, families with luggage',
    desc: 'A private transfer isn&rsquo;t just a faster ferry. It&rsquo;s a different kind of day: no 6am check-out to make the only good departure, no scrum at the ramp, no hauling suitcases across a hot port. You leave from a quiet harbor near your hotel and arrive at a quiet harbor near the next one.',
    notes: [
      ['You set the clock.', 'Late check-out, one more morning at the pool, then a 2pm departure &mdash; instead of building your whole day around a ferry timetable.'],
      ['Small ports, not the big ones.', 'Most crossings run from the closest practical harbor to your hotel, which usually means a shorter drive and no terminal at all.'],
      ['Swim stop optional.', 'On most routes we can add a stop at a beach or sea cave you can only reach by boat, and turn the transfer into the best half-day of the trip.'],
    ],
    take: 'This is the single upgrade my clients thank me for most, and it costs less than they expect when there are four or more of you.',
  },
  {
    num: '02', img: '/images/itinerary/wally-santorini.jpg', alt: 'A fast day boat crossing beneath the Santorini caldera cliffs', id: 'routes',
    h: 'The routes that work', tag: 'Neighbors, not marathons',
    bestfor: 'Sweet spot · crossings under about 90 minutes',
    desc: 'Private boats are at their best between islands that are genuinely close. Cross the Cyclades&rsquo; short gaps and you get a beautiful, comfortable ride; try to run Athens to Santorini on a small boat and you get an endurance test. These are the legs I book most.',
    notes: [
      ['Mykonos &harr; Paros &amp; Antiparos.', 'The workhorse. Also Mykonos &harr; Naxos, and Paros &harr; Naxos in barely any time at all.'],
      ['Sifnos &harr; Milos.', 'My favorite crossing in Greece. Short, sheltered on most days, and it links two islands whose ferry connection is genuinely thin &mdash; often a single awkward boat, or none at all.'],
      ['Santorini &harr; Milos.', 'The one that surprises people. Roughly two hours across open water on a fast boat, and it turns two islands that feel unrelated on a map into a natural pair.'],
      ['Santorini &harr; Folegandros or Ios.', 'The honeymoon move &mdash; a genuinely small island added to the trip without losing a day to the ferry.'],
      ['Longer legs, honestly.', 'Mykonos to Santorini or anything out of Athens is possible, but it&rsquo;s a long ride in open water. For those I&rsquo;ll usually point you at <a href="/hoper.html" style="color:var(--brass-lit);">a helicopter</a> instead.'],
    ],
    take: 'My rule: fly the long legs, sail the short ones. Helicopter from Athens, private boat between neighbors.',
  },
  {
    num: '03', img: '/images/transfers/technohull-santorini.jpg', alt: 'A captain at the helm of a black Technohull RIB off the Santorini coast', id: 'know',
    h: 'Good to know before you book', tag: 'The honest fine print',
    bestfor: 'Read this · before you commit to a date',
    desc: 'A private boat is a small boat, and the Aegean has opinions. None of this is a reason not to do it &mdash; it&rsquo;s just what separates a smooth transfer from a memorable one for the wrong reasons.',
    notes: [
      ['The Meltemi gets a vote.', 'In high summer the wind can push a crossing earlier in the day, change the route, or occasionally cancel it. I always build the plan so a cancelled boat doesn&rsquo;t cost you a hotel night.'],
      ['Luggage has limits.', 'Most boats handle a couple of large cases per cabin comfortably. If you&rsquo;re travelling heavy, tell me up front and I&rsquo;ll size the boat accordingly.'],
      ['Pricing is per boat, not per person.', 'Transfers start around &euro;1,000 for a standard crossing, and go up with distance, boat size, and any swim stops you add. Split between a family or two couples, it&rsquo;s a very different number than it sounds.'],
      ['The hack: make the transfer your boat day.', 'A private boat day around Milos runs about &euro;1,400 on its own. A transfer with swim stops built in lands in similar territory &mdash; so instead of paying for a boat day <i>and</i> a ferry ticket, you pay once and arrive on the next island at the end of it.'],
      ['Both ends need a car.', 'Harbors aren&rsquo;t hotels. When I arrange the boat, the transfer on each side is part of the booking, not an afterthought.'],
      ['Book it early in season.', 'Late June through early September, the good captains and the good boats are spoken for weeks out.'],
    ],
    take: 'Handled properly, it&rsquo;s the smoothest travel day of your trip. Handled casually, it&rsquo;s still a small boat in open water &mdash; so let&rsquo;s handle it properly.',
  },
];
---
<Layout
  canonical="private-boat-transfers.html"
  title="Private Boat Transfers in the Greek Islands | Suites With Keith"
  description="Skip the ferry line. I arrange private boat transfers between the Cyclades — Sifnos to Milos, Santorini to Folegandros, Mykonos to Paros — on your schedule, with cars waiting on both ends."
  preload="/images/transfers/private-boat-hero.jpg"
>

<!-- hero -->
<header class="hero" style="min-height:min(80svh,740px);">
  <img class="hero-img" src="/images/transfers/private-boat-hero.jpg" alt="A black day boat running fast beneath the Santorini caldera cliffs" width="1800" height="1200" fetchpriority="high" />
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Services &middot; private boat transfers</p>
    <h1 class="display-xl" style="margin-top:18px;">Island to island,<br><em>on your schedule</em></h1>
    <p class="sub">You saw the boat. Here&rsquo;s how it actually works &mdash; a private transfer between islands, timed to your check-out, with a car waiting on both ends.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn" href="#inquire" data-gtag-label="start_planning" data-gtag-location="hero">Ask me about a transfer</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost on-shadow" href="#routes" style="border-color:rgba(242,239,230,.4); color:var(--band-ink);" data-gtag-label="boat_routes" data-gtag-location="hero">See the routes</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- intro -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container intro-grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="deck" style="max-width:44ch;">The fast boats sell out, the schedules shift, and a two-island week can quietly cost you two full travel days at the port.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:20px; max-width:58ch;">If you&rsquo;ve read my <a href="/greek-ferry-rules.html" style="color:var(--brass);">ferry rules</a>, you already know the problem. A private boat transfer solves it. Instead of dragging your luggage down to Santorini&rsquo;s ferry port at 7am, or into the scrum at Mykonos&rsquo; new port, a captain meets you at a small harbor near your hotel, you leave when you&rsquo;re ready, and you&rsquo;re on the next island in the time it takes to have lunch. On the right route it&rsquo;s genuinely the nicest hour of the trip.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:14px; max-width:58ch;">These are arranged individually &mdash; boat, captain, route, and timing all depend on your islands and your dates. Tell me where you&rsquo;re going and I&rsquo;ll price it and hold it for you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <dl class="kv">
        <div class="kv-row"><dt>Transfers from</dt><dd><b>&euro;1,000</b> per boat, not per person</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row"><dt>Typical crossing</dt><dd><b>30&ndash;90 minutes</b> between neighbors</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row"><dt>Best crossings</dt><dd>Sifnos &harr; Milos &middot; Mykonos &harr; Paros &middot; Santorini &harr; Folegandros &middot; Santorini &harr; Milos</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row"><dt>Included</dt><dd>Boat &amp; captain &middot; cars on both ends &middot; luggage handled &middot; optional swim stop</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{cards.map((c, i) => (
  <section class={`section${i % 2 === 0 ? ' band on-shadow' : ''}`} id={c.id} style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class={`hc-grid${i % 2 ? ' flip' : ''}`}>
        <figure class="reveal hc-media">
          <img src={c.img} alt={c.alt} width="1800" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </figure>
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="stamp plain" style={`font-weight:700; color:${i % 2 === 0 ? 'var(--brass-lit)' : 'var(--brass)'};`}>No. {c.num}</span>
          <h2 class="display-l" style="margin-top:12px;" set:html={c.h} />
          <p class="deck" style="margin-top:10px; font-size:1.05rem;" set:html={c.tag} />
          <p class="stamp plain small-meta" set:html={c.bestfor} />
          <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:18px;" set:html={c.desc} />
          <div style="margin-top:22px;">
            {c.notes.map(([b, t]) => (
              <p class="hc-note"><b set:html={b} /> <span set:html={t} /></p>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:26px;"><p set:html={c.take} /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
))}

<!-- yachts -->
<section class="section" id="yachts" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Going bigger</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">If you&rsquo;d rather have a yacht</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="body-2 reveal" style="max-width:60ch;">A transfer boat is the practical end of this. The other end is a crewed yacht &mdash; a sailing catamaran or a motor yacht with a captain, a chef, and cabins &mdash; chartered by the day or by the week, with the islands as your route rather than your destination.</p>
    <p class="body-2 reveal" style="margin-top:14px; max-width:60ch;">It&rsquo;s a different budget and a different kind of trip, but it answers the same instinct: seeing the Cyclades from the water instead of from a ferry queue. If that&rsquo;s what you&rsquo;re actually picturing, say so in the note below and I&rsquo;ll put options in front of you.</p>
    <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:26px; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:14px;">
      <a class="btn" href="#inquire" data-gtag-label="yacht_charter_inquiry" data-gtag-location="yacht_band">Ask about a charter</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/hoper.html" data-gtag-label="hoper_cross_link" data-gtag-location="yacht_band">Or fly it instead</a>
    </div>
    <div class="verdict reveal" style="margin-top:44px;">
      <p>Nobody remembers the ferry fondly. Here&rsquo;s the math I keep coming back to: a private boat day on Milos is about &euro;1,400 all by itself. Book the Sifnos crossing with a couple of swim stops instead, and you&rsquo;ve bought the same day out on the water &mdash; and it drops you at your next hotel at the end of it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- two ways in -->
<section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">The boat is one piece</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">Where are you starting from?</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="choose reveal">
      <div class="choose-col">
        <span class="eyebrow">Nothing booked yet</span>
        <h3>Hotels are where I start</h3>
        <p class="lead">Hotel bookings through me are complimentary &mdash; I&rsquo;m paid by the hotel, and you get preferred-partner extras on top of the same rate: typically a space-available upgrade, daily breakfast, and a hotel credit. The boat, the cars, and the timing get built around the rooms.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:24px; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:14px;">
          <a class="btn" href="#inquire" data-gtag-label="plan_whole_trip" data-gtag-location="boat_paths">Have me plan the trip</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/services.html" data-gtag-label="services_link" data-gtag-location="boat_paths">What I do &amp; what it costs</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="choose-col">
        <span class="eyebrow">Already booked your hotel?</span>
        <h3>I can still handle everything around it</h3>
        <p class="lead">Nothing gets cancelled or rebooked &mdash; I work around what you&rsquo;ve confirmed and build the days on top of it: the boat between islands, the cars on both ends, the tables, the timing. Send me the confirmation and your dates; that&rsquo;s all I need to start.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:24px; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px 28px;">
          <a class="btn" href="#inquire" data-gtag-label="already_booked_inquiry" data-gtag-location="boat_paths">Send me your dates</a>
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top:16px; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px 28px;">
          <a class="pb-link" href="/already-booked-santorini.html">What I take on &middot; Santorini &rarr;</a>
          <a class="pb-link" href="/already-booked-mykonos.html">What I take on &middot; Mykonos &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<Ask
  subject="Inquiry — private boat transfers"
  page="private-boat-transfers"
  placeholder="Sifnos to Milos, June 12 &mdash; two of us"
  deck="Tell me the two islands and the dates &mdash; I&rsquo;ll come back with the right boat and a real price."
  dark
/>

</Layout>

<style>
  .intro-grid { display: grid; gap: 44px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .intro-grid { grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: 80px; } }
  .intro-grid > * { min-width: 0; }

  .hc-grid { display: grid; gap: 40px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hc-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr; gap: 64px; }
    .hc-grid.flip .hc-media { order: 2; }
  }
  .hc-grid > * { min-width: 0; }
  .hc-media { margin: 0; }
  .hc-media img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4/3; object-fit: cover; }
  .small-meta { display: block; margin-top: 14px; font-size: .66rem; }
  .band .small-meta { color: var(--band-ash); }
  .hc-note { font-size: .96rem; line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 13px; padding-left: 16px; position: relative; color: var(--ash); }
  .band .hc-note { color: var(--band-ash); }
  .hc-note::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .62em; width: 4px; height: 4px; background: var(--brass); }
  .band .hc-note::before { background: var(--brass-lit); }
  .hc-note b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .band .hc-note b { color: var(--band-ink); }
  .band .verdict { border-left-color: var(--brass-lit); }
  .pb-link { font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brass); text-decoration: none; }
  .pb-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
